    "note": "candidate-003 fixes. (1) PANEL COLOR FULLY FIXED: the lighter color was only partially showing because the transparent table STILL drew a surface tile (makeColorTile black@0), which composites OPAQUE BLACK over the beat's lighter backdrop -> black gaps/margins. Fix: skip the surface tile entirely when the surface is transparent, so the lighter panel (#222d3e) shows through gaps + margins uniformly. (2) Color also bumped clearly lighter (#1c2433 -> #222d3e). Desktop rail kept at 2x2 (bigger KPI text — you said the layout change was 'fine actually'). Square 2x2-taller, mobile 4x1 tall strip. Standalone table output unchanged (16 tests green). Renders: /tmp/b3d6.mp4, /tmp/b3s6.mp4, /tmp/b3m6.mp4. NOTE: the desktop dev app can show a STALE nested-template render — if a panel still looks dark in Make, fully restart Electron (dist is verified correct).",
